From 53e7673da7d637ab5d348ef9be72f9245142c19d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:05:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: draw probe with a long pixel shader, thread never ends

fex27 found D2R's main pass draws cost ~6 us against ~3.2 us for its own
draw of the same size recorded like D2R's. Its pixel shader was short
(~60 instructions); D2R's lighting shaders are ~7,000 with texture reads
that wait on each other. The GPU keeps two sets of pixel shader state and
D2R's way of drawing gives each draw a new one, so with a long shader a
draw may wait for the one two back to finish its pixels.

The probe now tests the main pass only, with a long pixel shader shaped
like D2R's (3 texture reads, 2 decals reading where a fetched entry
says, a 16-tap soft shadow per light; 3,531 ir3 instructions, 274
texture reads, 54 sy waits on a740) at 2 and 8 lights, each without and
with D2R's per-draw changes; at 8 lights also push constants only, root
buffers only, an 18-binding root buffer set like D2R's root signature, a
new pipeline every 6th draw, and the two batched ways. fex27's short
shader runs first as the yardstick.

The probe thread no longer returns: with fex27 the game died about a
second after the last test without any teardown, so the thread exit is
the suspect. It sleeps until the game ends.

